    "description": "UAMD-2-Srtd (Serrated): Laffs\n\nUndectectable Additive Manufactured Dagger. Second model; serrated variant.\n\nA angled spine 3DP dagger with a wide, tanto styled blade tip. Simple to print and use. Has 16 angled teeth to aid in ripping meat.\n\nMelt it down after use.\n\n\n\nPrinter Used: Ender 3 V2\n\nFilament Used: PLA+ (More durable if printed in CF Nylon, though melting it down after use would be a bit more difficult.)\n\nPrint Settings:\n\nExtruder: 220C \nBed: 56C \nFirst Layer Print Height: .2mm \nStandard Layer Height: .12mm\nWall Thickness: .40 \nWall Perimeters: 8+\nInfill: 50%+\n\n\n\nNote: The original UAMD-2 can be found here: https://odysee.com/@FFFTech:3/UAMD2:d\n\n\n\nNote: Yes, ik its small. (165mm) That's the idea you little shits >.> \n\n\n\nIntelligence is our greatest trait, violence is a close second. Best to start embracing it, for how else could we have conquered this planet?",
